WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:00.950
The half volley.

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.050
It's also called hitting it on the bounce.

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:07.530
You can think of the half volley as

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.590
taking the ball right where it lands, using the low-ball stance,

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.290
and using the pace of the bounce.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.250
It's a way of handling a transition ball.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:19.280
The key to practising it is reading and catching where the ball will land.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.860
Before hitting,

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.940
we can first do a covering drill.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.760
After the split step, quickly lower your weight,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.640
lower the racket,

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.500
face down,

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.460
use small steps to fine-tune your distance to the ball,

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.700
watch the ball hard,

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.820
and cover the ball with the racket the instant it lands.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.320
We feed balls with the ball machine

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.620
and repeat this find-and-cover drill.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.430
Once you can find the ball reliably,

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:44.290
keep everything else the same,

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:45.570
turn the racket face over,

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.290
and go from covering the ball to sweeping it.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:55.480
Once you have this detail,

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.940
we put it into the forehand and backhand framework

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.140
and practise each with the ball machine.
